  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1102 AM MST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nMean western NOAM ridging will support mild and dry weather as \nPac flow continues aloft. Weak/skirting impulses will support cool\nfronts at times to knock temps down a few degrees. Temps will be \nabove normal in the period with the warmest days being this \nweekend, particularity Sunday when highs will average 20 degrees \nabove normal. The only expected impact in the period attm is for \nareas of fog toward central SD tonight. Moist BL with ESE upslope \nflow will support low clouds and fog later tonight there with fog \nand low clouds possibly shifting as far west as K2WX to KRAP. Any \nfog will quickly burn off Friday morning with temps recovering \nnicely by afternoon. Compact upper impulse will move through \nsouthern Canada on Friday and the the only impact from this system\nwill be breezy winds across NW SD Sat. Another stronger trough \nwill take a similar path across southern Canada on Sunday, \nsupporting cool front into the area. This will knock temps back \ndown into the 50s and 60s for Monday. Otherwise, no other impacts \nexpected. This pattern looks to continue beyond the forecast \nperiod into the following weekend.",
